Subject: realtek: rteth (rtl838x_eth) NIC path: RTL930x doorbell, TX reclaim, overload (#60 #65)

Measured: docs/NAT.md "NIC path" and #60/#65 (per step, 3 runs each).
- TX doorbell (RTL930x only): one writel_relaxed of a cached DMA_IF_CTRL per kick; no read-poll,
  regmap lock or ktime. SDK r9300_nicTxFetch_set writes the field without a poll; the poll stays
  for RTL838x/839x/931x (empty-read workaround), now in rteth_83xx_tx_kick.
- TX stats per ring under the txq lock + ndo_get_stats64; tx_lock only guards the RMW doorbell.
- TX reclaim: napi_consume_skb (skb cache, direct page_pool recycle) instead of dev_consume_skb_any.
- Overload collapse fix: TX got one ring per RX poll (reclaim only at poll start, 1G CPU port):
  - reclaim inline in xmit when the ring is full, stop the queue only if still full;
  - TX ring 32 -> 128 (two polls of frames), wake at 16 free;
  - doorbell at least every 16 frames of an xmit_more batch (fraglist GRO segments).
- Generic parts (reclaim, ring size, kick batch) apply to all families; only RTL930x is tested.
